   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law, in relation to exempting the Buchanan Engine\nCompany No. 1 from the requirement that the percentage of non-resident fire\ndepartment members not exceed forty-five percent of the membership",
    "basePrintNo": "S5886",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5886-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §10-1006, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5886\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law, in relation to exempting the Buchanan\nEngine Company No. 1 from the requirement that the percentage of non-re-\nsident fire department members not exceed forty-five percent of the\nmembership\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExempts the Buchanan Engine Company No. 1 from the requirement that the\npercentage of non-resident fire department members not exceed forty-five\npercent of the membership\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the village law to provide that the Buchanan Engine\nCompany No. 1 is exempt from the provision requiring the percentage of\nnon-residents in a volunteer fire organization to not exceed forty-five\npercent.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA fire company requires a certain amount of members to ensure it is\ncapable of responding to emergencies safely and efficiently.  Individ-\nuals who are otherwise competent and willing to serve the village of\nBuchanan should not be barred from serving as a member of the Buchanan\nEngine Company No. 1 simply because they live outside the village, or\nhave relocated out of Buchanan. This legislation will best allow the\nBuchanan Engine Company No. 1 to fill its ranks, and ensure it is able\nto continue to provide comprehensive emergency protection to the village\nof Buchanan.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
